1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,500
You know, I'm thinking about letting Emma have her first cookie.

2
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:07,820
Her first cookie?

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:09,090
She has cookies all the time.

4
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,410
I've never given her a cookie.

5
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:15,020
- Have you? - No.

6
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:17,250
No. And for the record,

7
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:19,940
I've also never given her frosting from a can.

8
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:25,010
Hey, Rach, the adoption agency needs letters of recommendation...

9
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:26,940
...and we wondered if you would write one for us?

10
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:29,780
Of course. I would be honored.

11
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:30,340
Thank you.

12
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:36,800
I think there's been an oversight.

13
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:38,850
We would have asked you.

14
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,290
We thought you wouldn't be interested.

15
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:42,160
It's just that we don't think of you

16
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:45,040
as really being so much with the words.

17
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:50,680
Clearly, we were wrong.

18
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:53,690
I got a lot of nice stuff

19
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:55,140
to say about you guys, okay?

20
00:00:55,190 --> 00:00:57,770
I know how much you want to have a baby...

21
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,770
...and I would love to help you get one.

22
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:04,080
You know what? Joey. Then we want you to do it.

23
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:07,040
Thank you. All right. Let me see how I'm gonna start.

24
00:01:08,630 --> 00:01:10,920
"Dear Baby Adoption Decider People...."

25
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:15,930
So excited about your letter.

26
00:01:18,450 --> 00:01:20,410
- Hey. - Hey, Phoebe.

27
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:23,750
- Wow, don't you look nice. - Yes, I do.

28
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:27,900
Today's Mike and my one-year anniversary.

29
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:29,700
What's it the anniversary of?

30
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:33,760
Your first date, your first kiss, first time you had sex?

31
00:01:33,810 --> 00:01:34,940
Yeah.

32
00:01:36,890 --> 00:01:39,670
So you must be going somewhere fancy to celebrate.

33
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,430
A Knicks game.

34
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,290
Aren't you a little overdressed?

35
00:01:44,790 --> 00:01:47,180
I've never had a one-year anniversary before...

36
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:50,150
...so no matter where we go, I'm wearing something fancy...

37
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:52,190
...I'm gonna put on my finest jewelry...

38
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,480
...and we're gonna have sex in a public restroom.

39
00:01:55,730 --> 00:01:57,180
You guys do that?

40
00:01:57,230 --> 00:01:59,730
Chandler won't even have sex in our bathroom.

41
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,760
That's where people make number two.

42
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,020
Friends S10E05 The One Where Rachel's Other Sister Babysits

43
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:04,680
So, you know, I have a little time

44
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,500
if you want to....

45
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:12,210
I'd love to, but I really have to grade these papers.

46
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:14,260
Fine. It's fine.

47
00:03:14,890 --> 00:03:16,860
I'll just shower by myself.

48
00:03:18,250 --> 00:03:21,660
B...
B...

49
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:25,100
You gave a B to a Pottery Barn catalog.

50
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:26,690
Well, it had some good ideas.

51
00:03:26,690 --> 00:03:27,460
Take off your shirt.

52
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:33,170
- Damn it. - Rachel, open up! It's your sister!

53
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:35,480
I have to talk to you.

54
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:37,940
Hi, Amy.

55
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:45,360
- You're not Rachel. - Still sharp as a tack.

56
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:49,360
Charlie, this is Rachel's sister Amy.

57
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,680
Amy, this is Charlie.

58
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,660
- Hi. Nice to meet you. - Hi, hi.

59
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:54,140
And you are?

60
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:03,400
Ross? I grew up on your block?

61
00:04:04,270 --> 00:04:06,630
We had Thanksgiving together last year?

62
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:08,900
I had a baby with your sister?

63
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,490
No. I....

64
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:15,680
Did I buy a falafel from you yesterday?

65
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:20,590
Yes. Yes, you did.

66
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:28,450
Hi, Rachel. Here's your sister Amy.

67
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,500
She thinks I need pec implants.

68
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,240
Amy? Hi.

69
00:04:34,350 --> 00:04:36,710
- You remember Joey. - Yeah. Hey, sure.

70
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:39,350
- The Days of our Lives guy. - That's right, yeah.

71
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:41,500
You are not good.

72
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:46,010
Always nice to meet a fan.

73
00:04:47,230 --> 00:04:49,320
So, now, what are you doing here?

74
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,120
Well, I have huge news.

75
00:04:51,370 --> 00:04:52,940
Sorry, hold on. Let me check on the baby.

76
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:55,420
This is important. Can't Ella wait?

77
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:57,950
Her name is Emma.

78
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:00,600
Why did you change it?

79
00:05:00,650 --> 00:05:02,380
Ella was so much prettier.

80
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:04,690
What do I know?

81
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:07,180
I just sell Middle Eastern food from a cart.

82
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:10,100
Hey, your English is getting better.

83
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:16,430
- Oh, my God. - I know.

84
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:18,160
She may be the hottest girl I've ever hated.

85
00:05:19,690 --> 00:05:21,030
What you working on?

86
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:23,330
Monica and Chandler's recommendation.

87
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:25,010
I want it to sound smart,

88
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:26,970
but I don't know any big words or anything.

89
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:29,070
Why don't you use your thesaurus?

90
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,360
What did I just say?

91
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,260
Watch.

92
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:37,440
Here, highlight the word you want to change,

93
00:05:37,490 --> 00:05:39,360
go under "tools" ...

94
00:05:39,410 --> 00:05:42,200
...and the thesaurus generates-- Gives.

95
00:05:43,770 --> 00:05:46,260
Gives a whole list of choices.

96
00:05:46,310 --> 00:05:48,860
You can pick the word that sounds smartest.

97
00:05:48,910 --> 00:05:51,520
My God, that's great. I'm smart.

98
00:05:51,570 --> 00:05:53,010
No, no, I'm:

99
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:56,040
"Brainy, bright, clever." I love this thing!

100
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:58,230
Look out, ladies!

101
00:05:58,230 --> 00:06:00,360
Joey Tribbiani's got the whole package!

102
00:06:02,580 --> 00:06:03,790
God...

103
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:06,640
...so beautiful.

104
00:06:06,690 --> 00:06:08,590
I know, isn't she?

105
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:11,010
No, I was talking about your bedding.

106
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:16,000
All right, what's your news, Amy?

107
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:18,600
Well...

108
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:20,570
...I'm getting married.

109
00:06:21,070 --> 00:06:23,120
Wow! Oh, my God!

110
00:06:23,630 --> 00:06:25,740
- To who? - This guy.

111
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:30,260
