112
00:06:32,970 --> 00:06:36,190
- And...? - And it's on Fifth.

113
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:39,390
And the elevator opens up right into the living room.

114
00:06:39,650 --> 00:06:42,840
- No, what's he like? - Oh, he's okay.

115
00:06:44,610 --> 00:06:46,730
Do you remember my old boyfriend Mark?

116
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:49,370
- Yeah. - It's his dad.

117
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:55,210
- Wow, so he's gotta be-- - Old? Yeah.

118
00:06:57,010 --> 00:06:57,960
But he travels a lot,

119
00:06:58,010 --> 00:06:59,290
so he's hardly ever there.

120
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:03,460
Sweetie, I gotta tell you,

121
00:07:03,470 --> 00:07:05,140
it sounds a little bit like...

122
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:07,490
...you like the apartment more than you like--

123
00:07:07,610 --> 00:07:08,610
Myron.

124
00:07:09,250 --> 00:07:10,690
Yeah, I told you he was old.

125
00:07:11,930 --> 00:07:13,050
Sit down.

126
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,440
Honey, you know...

127
00:07:15,830 --> 00:07:19,060
...l once also almost married somebody that I didn't love.

128
00:07:19,110 --> 00:07:21,480
- Do you remember Barry? - Remember him?

129
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:24,510
God, we used to make out all the time after you went to sleep.

130
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:29,700
Sometimes just nodding is okay.

131
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:32,450
But anyway, listen.

132
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:36,420
Not marrying Barry was the best decision that I ever, ever made.

133
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:38,550
Honey, Amy, you deserve true love.

134
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,960
Your soul mate is out there somewhere.

135
00:07:41,010 --> 00:07:46,060
Someone that is your age, that is smart, that is fun...

136
00:07:46,110 --> 00:07:48,230
...and that you care about.

137
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:51,530
You're right.

138
00:07:52,090 --> 00:07:53,930
- You're right. I'm gonna do it. - Okay.

139
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:55,660
I'm gonna marry Myron

140
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,780
and keep looking for Mr. Right.

141
00:08:00,570 --> 00:08:01,920
Okay, let's keep talking.

142
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:13,780
Excuse me. Anniversary.

143
00:08:14,930 --> 00:08:17,210
Excuse me. Anniversary.

144
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:23,110
Sir, could you move your nachos?

145
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,530
They're in my seat.

146
00:08:26,810 --> 00:08:28,390
It's my anniversary.

147
00:08:33,250 --> 00:08:34,590
Here we are.

148
00:08:35,150 --> 00:08:37,120
I can't believe it's been a whole year.

149
00:08:37,170 --> 00:08:38,120
I know.

150
00:08:38,550 --> 00:08:40,430
This has been the best year....

151
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:44,140
This has been the best year of my life!

152
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:45,050
Me too!

153
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:47,820
I never thought I could love someone this much!

154
00:08:48,070 --> 00:08:49,760
I feel the same way!

155
00:08:49,810 --> 00:08:52,000
You're so generous and kind,

156
00:08:52,050 --> 00:08:54,260
and you're amazing in bed!

157
00:08:58,350 --> 00:08:59,870
It's our anniversary.

158
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:04,600
Knicks fans, please turn your attention

159
00:09:04,650 --> 00:09:06,400
to the big screen on the scoreboard.

160
00:09:06,450 --> 00:09:09,070
Someone has a special question to ask.

161
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:18,050
How lame. It's so tacky and impersonal.

162
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:19,200
Really?

163
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:21,290
It's the worst way to propose.

164
00:09:24,530 --> 00:09:25,730
Excuse me.

165
00:09:29,830 --> 00:09:32,220
I finished my recommendation. Here.

166
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:36,120
And I think you'll be very, very happy.

167
00:09:36,670 --> 00:09:37,820
It's the longest I ever spent on a computer

168
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:39,140
without looking at porn.

169
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,990
I don't understand.

170
00:09:45,590 --> 00:09:47,820
Some of the words a little too sophisticated for you?

171
00:09:49,330 --> 00:09:51,130
It doesn't make any sense.

172
00:09:51,310 --> 00:09:52,420
Well, of course it does.

173
00:09:52,470 --> 00:09:55,100
It's smart. I used a thesaurus.

174
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,240
On every word?

175
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,130
Yep.

176
00:10:02,470 --> 00:10:05,340
All right, what was this sentence originally?

177
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:09,380
"They are warm, nice people with big hearts."

178
00:10:09,430 --> 00:10:10,470
And that became,

179
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:14,740
"They are humid, prepossessing Homo sapiens...

180
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:17,640
...with full-sized aortic pumps."

181
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:23,050
Yeah. Yeah. And hey, I really mean it, dude.

182
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:27,290
All right, Joey, I don't think we can use this.

183
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:29,840
- Why not? - Well, because you signed it:

184
00:10:29,890 --> 00:10:32,170
"Baby Kangaroo Tribbiani."

185
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,820
Why don't you stop worrying about sounding smart

186
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:41,200
and just be yourself.

187
00:10:41,250 --> 00:10:44,050
You don't need a thesaurus. Just write from here.

188
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:45,830
Your full-sized aortic pump.

189
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:53,660
- Amy. Hi. - I took your advice.

190
00:10:53,710 --> 00:10:56,820
- I left Myron. - Good for you!

191
00:10:56,870 --> 00:10:59,740
I know. I'm Erin Brockovich.

192
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,290
Yes, you are.

193
00:11:04,810 --> 00:11:07,290
- I'm so proud of you. - Thank you.

194
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,460
So can I stay with you?

195
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:16,200
But Erin Brockovich had her own house.

196
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:21,460
Look who's back.

197
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,240
Why do you have bags?

198
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:24,930
Rach,why does she have bags?

199
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:26,930
I'm staying with you guys.

200
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:29,050
- What? - We're gonna be roomies!

201
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:30,160
Come on.

202
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:41,410
- You slept out here? - Yeah.

203
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:43,400
Amy kept kicking me in her sleep,

204
00:11:43,450 --> 00:11:45,220
yelling, "Myron, get off!"

205
00:11:46,670 --> 00:11:48,760
But we're getting rid of her, right?

206
00:11:48,810 --> 00:11:50,440
Rachel,please tell me we're getting rid of her?

207
00:11:50,570 --> 00:11:53,260
- Joey, I can't do that. - Oh, come on.

208
00:11:53,310 --> 00:11:55,200
Last night I was finishing off a pizza,

209
00:11:55,250 --> 00:11:56,310
and she said

210
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:58,410
"A moment on the lips, forever on the hips."

211
00:12:00,090 --> 00:12:02,150
I don't need that kind of talk in my house!

212
00:12:03,010 --> 00:12:05,500
Joey, look, I know that she's difficult...

213
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:08,200
...but I think it's really good that she's here.

214
00:12:09,150 --> 00:12:12,210
Because we'll appreciate it more when she's gone?

215
00:12:13,910 --> 00:12:16,510
No, it's just-- Look, when I first moved to this city,

216
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:18,010
I was a lot like her.

217
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:20,530
I was spoiled, self-centered.

218
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:22,700
And you guys really took care of me.

219
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:24,540
Yeah. Monica made us.

220
00:12:26,230 --> 00:12:28,780
Well, whatever. I really appreciate it...

221
00:12:28,830 --> 00:12:31,730
...because I don't think I would be the person I am today...

222
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:33,520
...if it wasn't for you guys.

223
00:12:33,570 --> 00:12:35,340
So I want to help Amy

224
00:12:35,390 --> 00:12:36,300
the way you guys helped me.

225
00:12:36,350 --> 00:12:37,870
And I know it's gonna take patience,

226
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:38,860
but that's okay.

227
00:12:40,690 --> 00:12:42,960
- Good morning. - Yeah.

228
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:46,850
That's what I'm wearing today.

229
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,220
That's why I hung it on the door.

230
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:50,970
Oh, sweetie, you can't pull this off.

231
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:56,480
You know what?

232
00:12:56,530 --> 00:12:59,430
I was thinking that maybe now would be a good time...

233
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:03,350
...for us to sit down and, you know, talk about your future.

234
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,620
Oh, I can't, honey.

235
00:13:04,670 --> 00:13:06,370
I'm gonna go get my eyebrows shaped.

236
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:07,840
I am not happy.

237
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:12,350
Sure you want to eat that?

238
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:17,510
I'm curvy and I like it!

239
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:23,620
- Hi. - Hi.

240
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:26,920
I just had the worst anniversary ever.

241
00:13:26,970 --> 00:13:27,940
I doubt that.

242
00:13:27,990 --> 00:13:29,220
Tell her about us last year.

243
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:32,280
Well, I bought Chandler a $500 watch,

244
00:13:32,330 --> 00:13:34,480
and he wrote me a rap song.

245
00:13:36,870 --> 00:13:39,110
- Seriously? - Word.

246
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,980
Mine was worse than that.

247
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,290
Well, what happened?

248
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:45,370
We were at the game.

249
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:48,320
This guy proposed to his girlfriend on the big screen thing.

250
00:13:48,370 --> 00:13:49,540
That is so tacky.

251
00:13:49,590 --> 00:13:51,330
Well, that's what I said.

252
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:53,610
But it turns out Mike was planning on

253
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:55,830
proposing to me the same way last night.

254
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:58,160
Oh, my God. Mike was gonna propose?

255
00:13:58,210 --> 00:13:59,130
That's huge.

256
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:00,290
Do you want to marry him?

257
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,470
Yeah, I really do. Yes.

258
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:05,710
But after I dumped on the way he was gonna do it...

259
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:07,390
...l don't think he'll ever ask again.

260
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:09,830
I said no in Barbados, and now this?

261
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,090
She's right. If I were a guy and....

262
00:14:17,830 --> 00:14:20,290
Did I just say, "lf I were a guy"?

263
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:23,530
You don't need him to propose to you.

264
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:24,950
Maybe you could propose to him.

265
00:14:25,510 --> 00:14:27,190
Oh, I don't know.

266
00:14:27,190 --> 00:14:29,070
I don't know. Isn't that a little desperate?

267
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,740
I proposed to Chandler.

268
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:36,580
All right, moving on.

269
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:38,810
I don't think it was desperate.

270
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:39,940
It was amazing.

271
00:14:39,990 --> 00:14:40,860
Thank you.

272
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:43,190
Well, do you think I should propose?

273
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,440
I think it could be kind of great.

274
00:14:45,490 --> 00:14:46,330
Absolutely.

275
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:47,690
You'll love the feeling.

276
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:48,840
There's nothing like it.

277
00:14:51,950 --> 00:14:54,890
Okay. Okay. So how should I do it?

278
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:57,110
How about at a game on the big screen?

279
00:14:57,990 --> 00:15:00,090
How about at a Foot Locker?

280
00:15:01,910 --> 00:15:04,050
What? What, he obviously thinks

281
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:06,290
that's a nice way to be proposed to.

282
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,190
Plus, he'd never suspect it.

283
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,620
Yeah, that does make sense.

284
00:15:10,070 --> 00:15:12,410
Okay, now, would you two like that?

285
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:13,510
Sounds good to me.

286
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:15,900
But what would a guy think?

287
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:21,260
- Nana's on the phone. - Wow.

288
00:15:21,650 --> 00:15:22,570
That's interesting,

289
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:24,650
since she died seven years ago.

290
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,780
She did?

291
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:29,430
Who got her condo in Boca?

292
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:31,730
Hello?

293
00:15:33,090 --> 00:15:34,480
It's our nanny.

294
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,490
Hi.

295
00:15:36,950 --> 00:15:41,430
Oh, God, I hope you feel better. Okay. Bye.

296
00:15:41,930 --> 00:15:43,570
That's Molly. She's sick.

297
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:44,770
Can you watch Emma today?

298
00:15:44,820 --> 00:15:46,950
I can't. I have back-to-back classes.

299
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,410
Did Molly say what she had?

300
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:50,110
Because my throat's been hurting.

301
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:51,570
Menstrual cramps.

302
00:15:53,830 --> 00:15:55,690
I don't think that's what this is.

303
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:59,040
Can any of you watch Emma?

304
00:15:59,090 --> 00:16:00,300
No, I'm sorry, sweetie.

305
00:16:00,350 --> 00:16:02,840
No, I've got work, and then I'm proposing.

306
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:05,810
Great. Shoot. What am I gonna do?

307
00:16:05,990 --> 00:16:07,470
Well, I could do it.

308
00:16:08,190 --> 00:16:09,230
Well, actually....

309
00:16:09,290 --> 00:16:11,100
Can I talk to you for a second?

310
00:16:13,190 --> 00:16:16,390
I do not want her babysitting our child.

311
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:17,150
Why not?

312
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:19,630
For one thing, she keeps calling her Ella.

313
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,180
Ella's a nice name.

314
00:16:22,230 --> 00:16:23,650
Fine, we'll call the next one Ella.

315
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:25,390
- The next one? - Okay.

316
00:16:27,170 --> 00:16:30,200
I don't want her watching our baby.

317
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:33,460
Ross, I am trying to help her become a better person.

318
00:16:33,510 --> 00:16:35,450
This is a huge breakthrough for her.

319
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:37,400
She just offered to do something

320
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:38,750
for another human being.

321
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:41,330
You know, I don't know.

322
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:42,390
Ross, I'm telling you...

323
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:46,640
...she's giving up getting her eyebrows shaped to do this, all right?

324
00:16:46,690 --> 00:16:47,780
Do you understand

325
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:50,140
how important that is in our world?

326
00:16:51,710 --> 00:16:54,800
Listen, I couldn't help but overhear,

327
00:16:55,150 --> 00:16:56,760
because I was trying to.

328
00:16:58,140 --> 00:16:59,780
Listen, let me do this.

329
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:01,350
I really want to help you guys out.

330
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:04,140
And plus, Rachel's been so wonderful to me.

331
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,540
- Absolutely. - Oh, great!

332
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:11,480
So how much does it pay?

333
00:17:18,290 --> 00:17:19,540
Hi,Joe.

334
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:20,780
How's the second draft of the letter coming?

335
00:17:20,830 --> 00:17:21,720
Great. I'm finished.

336
00:17:21,770 --> 00:17:23,410
In fact, I just dropped it off at the agency.

337
00:17:26,310 --> 00:17:28,050
- You dropped it off? - Yeah.

338
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:29,100
Can we read it?

339
00:17:29,150 --> 00:17:30,770
Can you print out another copy?

340
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,470
No can do, amigo.

341
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:35,300
No, I didn't use the computer.

342
00:17:35,350 --> 00:17:37,540
It felt more personal to handwrite it.

343
00:17:38,740 --> 00:17:41,010
- You handwrote it? - Yeah, and don't worry.

344
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:43,350
I didn't try to sound smart at all.

345
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:45,750
See you later.

346
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:47,600
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

347
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:50,120
That letter is gonna go in our file.

348
00:17:50,170 --> 00:17:51,860
We're never gonna get a kid.

349
00:17:51,910 --> 00:17:53,840
We're gonna be one of those old couples...

350
00:17:53,890 --> 00:17:57,030
...that collects orchids or has a lot of birds.

351
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:59,830
It's okay. You know what?

352
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:01,900
I will just call the agency

353
00:18:01,950 --> 00:18:03,640
and tell them to throw out the letter.

354
00:18:03,690 --> 00:18:04,770
Okay, good.

355
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:07,390
Hello, this is Chandler Bing.

356
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:09,130
Someone just dropped off

357
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:11,130
a handwritten recommendation letter and....

358
00:18:17,110 --> 00:18:18,070
Okay.

359
00:18:19,150 --> 00:18:21,380
Thank you. Goodbye.

360
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:24,170
We're screwed, aren't we?

361
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:24,850
You know what?

362
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:26,550
Just tell me on the way to the bird store.

363
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:30,120
- They loved it. - What?

364
00:18:30,170 --> 00:18:31,670
They thought it was very smart of us

365
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:33,980
to have a child write the letter.

366
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:37,360
They thought Joey was a child?

367
00:18:37,410 --> 00:18:40,310
She guessed 8, 9, based on his drawings.

368
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:46,330
- Hi. - Hey, what'd you guys do today?

369
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:48,040
Ella wanted to go out,

370
00:18:48,090 --> 00:18:51,150
so we went shopping and got some sushi.

371
00:18:51,870 --> 00:18:54,380
- That sounds like fun. - Yeah, not really.

372
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,550
Babies are dull.

373
00:18:58,430 --> 00:19:02,710
- Hey. Hi, how's my girl? - I'm fine.

374
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:05,930
And I got you a present

375
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:07,180
for letting me stay with you.

376
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:10,100
- Ready? - Yeah.

377
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,970
You pierced her ears?

378
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:18,880
Doesn't it make her nose look smaller?

379
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:27,180
You pierced her ears?

380
00:19:27,230 --> 00:19:29,310
How could you do this without telling me?

381
00:19:29,360 --> 00:19:30,650
If I had told you,

382
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:32,570
then it wouldn't have been a surprise, now would it?

383
00:19:33,770 --> 00:19:35,580
I think she looks cute.

384
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,710
But I am wrong.

385
00:19:39,250 --> 00:19:41,200
Oh, my God. Oh, my God. Here comes Ross.

386
00:19:41,250 --> 00:19:43,830
He's gonna flip out.

387
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:45,610
Why, did something happen

388
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:46,330
to his falafel cart?

389
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:49,650
- Hey, guys. - Ross!

390
00:19:49,790 --> 00:19:51,340
Hi, Emma.

391
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:53,540
Why is she wearing her hat so low?

392
00:19:53,590 --> 00:19:54,800
She can barely see.

393
00:19:54,850 --> 00:19:56,470
I don't really want her to see.

394
00:19:58,470 --> 00:19:59,770
Why not?

395
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:02,570
Because there are so many terrible sights in this world.

396
00:20:02,620 --> 00:20:05,940
Like war. Or that thing in Joey's refrigerator. Remember?

397
00:20:05,990 --> 00:20:08,590
It was in a milk carton, but it looked like meat?

398
00:20:10,220 --> 00:20:11,970
Come here.

399
00:20:12,510 --> 00:20:15,550
There she is. Hi.

400
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:19,700
- What? - Nothing.

401
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:22,720
Hi.

402
00:20:24,970 --> 00:20:25,910
What--?

403
00:20:37,100 --> 00:20:39,180
Please tell me those are clip-ons!

404
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:41,150
Oh, they're real.

405
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:44,110
Did she do this to her?

406
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,210
I told you

407
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:46,600
we shouldn't have left Emma with her!

408
00:20:46,650 --> 00:20:48,700
I know, I know. And you were right, Ross.

409
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:50,800
Okay? You are so irresponsible!

410
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:52,530
I am never letting you babysit again!

411
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:54,850
You know what? This kid needs me, okay?

412
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:57,310
She needs to have a cool, fun aunt.

413
00:20:57,360 --> 00:20:58,600
I'm a cool, fun aunt.

414
00:20:58,650 --> 00:20:59,780
Okay.

415
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:03,760
Hey! Monica can be cool and fun

416
00:21:03,810 --> 00:21:05,840
at organized indoor projects.

417
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:10,420
All I wanted to do was help you

418
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:12,260
try to figure out what to do with your life.

419
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:13,750
This is how you repay me?

420
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,290
I don't need you to help me.

421
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:17,290
Because I already know what I'm gonna do with my life.

422
00:21:17,290 --> 00:21:20,610
- Oh, yeah? Since when? - Since today.

423
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:26,530
I am going to be a baby stylist.

424
00:21:27,450 --> 00:21:30,140
- What? - That's not a thing!

425
00:21:31,710 --> 00:21:33,280
Well, it should be.

426
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:36,380
I'm gonna help babies learn how to accessorize...

427
00:21:36,430 --> 00:21:38,280
...what colors to wear,

428
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:39,900
what clothes are slimming.

429
00:21:39,950 --> 00:21:41,690
Babies don't care if they're slim!

430
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:43,310
Enter Amy.

431
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:47,160
Amy, l-- I just-- I just wanna--

432
00:21:47,210 --> 00:21:48,620
What? What are you gonna do?

433
00:21:50,230 --> 00:21:52,320
No more falafel for you!

434
00:22:05,390 --> 00:22:06,740
Great game, huh?

435
00:22:10,010 --> 00:22:11,500
Why do you keep looking at the screen?

436
00:22:11,550 --> 00:22:13,750
I'm not. I'm praying.

437
00:22:14,510 --> 00:22:16,490
Please let the Knicks win.

438
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,410
Thank you, Thor.

439
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:21,170
Where are you going?

440
00:22:21,490 --> 00:22:22,670
I'm going to the bathroom.

441
00:22:22,990 --> 00:22:24,170
Well, I think you should wait.

442
00:22:24,220 --> 00:22:24,970
Why?

443
00:22:26,150 --> 00:22:28,140
Well, if you don't hold it in,

444
00:22:28,190 --> 00:22:30,150
you don't get all the nutrients.

445
00:22:31,450 --> 00:22:33,830
Knicks fans, please turn your attention

446
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:35,750
to the big screen on the scoreboard.

447
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:38,990
Someone has a special question to ask.

448
00:22:41,630 --> 00:22:44,530
Mike Hannigan, will you marry me?

449
00:22:46,180 --> 00:22:50,070
Get a load of this. She's proposing to him!

450
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:53,260
Guess we know who wears the pants in that family.

451
00:22:53,910 --> 00:22:56,120
Well, that's not very enlightened.

452
00:23:00,540 --> 00:23:02,920
Boo us? Boo you!

453
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:13,130
Hello? Yeah, this is Joey Tribbiani.

454
00:23:13,570 --> 00:23:14,780
Oh, hi.

455
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:19,140
Well, I'm glad you liked my letter.

456
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:24,060
No, my mommy and daddy aren't home right now.

457
00:23:25,990 --> 00:23:27,490
Okay, bye-bye.

458
00:23:31,150 --> 00:23:32,410
She was nice.

459
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:36,850
Joey, get Amy's bags. She is moving out.

460
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,400
You're kicking me out?

461
00:23:40,450 --> 00:23:42,960
You put holes in my baby's ears.

462
00:23:43,010 --> 00:23:45,580
At least now people will know she's a girl!

463
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:50,890
I can't believe I ever even tried to help you.

464
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:53,230
- You are so beyond help! - You know what?

465
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:56,620
Ever since I got here, you have been nothing but negative.

466
00:23:56,670 --> 00:23:58,100
- Excuse me? - You didn't want me...

467
00:23:58,150 --> 00:24:00,570
...to marry the old guy with the great apartment.

468
00:24:01,010 --> 00:24:05,340
Then I tried to help your daughter de-emphasize her flaws...

469
00:24:05,950 --> 00:24:08,120
...and suddenly I'm the bad guy?

470
00:24:08,170 --> 00:24:09,630
Joey, where are those bags?

471
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:11,210
She has a lot of crap!

472
00:24:12,970 --> 00:24:14,660
You know? When I moved in here,

473
00:24:14,660 --> 00:24:16,350
I thought, "This will be so great.

474
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:19,620
Just us sisters back together again like when we were kids."

475
00:24:19,670 --> 00:24:21,680
Except without that stupid Jill.

476
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,120
Who has gotten fat, by the way.

477
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:28,270
Seriously?

478
00:24:28,940 --> 00:24:31,250
Mom said she gained, like, 15 pounds.

479
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:33,570
- Hips or thighs? - Ass and face.

480
00:24:35,410 --> 00:24:38,360
Oh, my God! I thought she was on Atkins.

481
00:24:38,470 --> 00:24:40,330
She was. Carbs found her.

482
00:24:45,030 --> 00:24:47,470
See? This is what I wanted.

483
00:24:47,950 --> 00:24:50,430
Two sisters talking about real stuff.

484
00:24:53,850 --> 00:24:56,020
Oh, I can give you that.

485
00:24:56,710 --> 00:24:58,280
- You can? - Yeah.

486
00:24:58,570 --> 00:25:01,570
I kept trying to make you a better person, but you're....

487
00:25:01,830 --> 00:25:04,840
You're already a pretty perfect version of what you are.

488
00:25:05,900 --> 00:25:07,580
Thank you.

489
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:10,690
You gotta admit, Emma does look cute.

490
00:25:12,590 --> 00:25:14,170
Did you just say, "Emma"?

491
00:25:14,220 --> 00:25:15,790
Oh, I'm sorry. Ella.

492
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:25,410
That woman didn't know what she was talking about, Mike.

493
00:25:25,410 --> 00:25:27,580
Obviously, you have balls.

494
00:25:29,340 --> 00:25:31,220
Please, let's forget the whole thing.

495
00:25:31,270 --> 00:25:32,290
I would love it.

496
00:25:32,290 --> 00:25:33,320
Consider it forgotten.

497
00:25:33,320 --> 00:25:34,180
Thank you.

498
00:25:35,250 --> 00:25:36,670
But just so you know....

499
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:40,210
However and whenever you decide to propose,

500
00:25:40,260 --> 00:25:41,950
I promise I'll say yes.

501
00:25:43,130 --> 00:25:45,500
Whether, you know, it's at a basketball game...

502
00:25:45,550 --> 00:25:47,490
...or in skywriting...

503
00:25:47,540 --> 00:25:50,460
...or, you know, like some lame guy in a cheesy movie...

504
00:25:50,510 --> 00:25:52,040
...who hides it in the cake.

505
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,760
It's in the cake, isn't it?

506
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:04,760
Where else would lame Mr. No Balls hide it?

507
00:26:05,650 --> 00:26:07,030
What's the matter with me?

508
00:26:07,080 --> 00:26:08,560
Why do I keep ruining this?

509
00:26:08,610 --> 00:26:10,000
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

510
00:26:10,050 --> 00:26:11,010
No, it's my fault.

511
00:26:11,060 --> 00:26:13,820
I keep trying to propose in these stupid ways...

512
00:26:13,870 --> 00:26:15,380
...and I just wanna tell you I love you,

513
00:26:15,430 --> 00:26:17,690
and I wanna spend my life with you....

514
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:23,460
I'm gonna do this now.

515
00:26:23,970 --> 00:26:25,310
Oh, my God.

516
00:26:28,970 --> 00:26:29,800
Phoebe, l--

517
00:26:29,850 --> 00:26:30,730
Wait. Oh, wait.

518
00:26:35,860 --> 00:26:36,800
Oh, no.

519
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:41,280
Okay.

520
00:26:42,590 --> 00:26:44,000
Ready? Okay.

521
00:26:47,840 --> 00:26:50,400
Phoebe, I love you.

522
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,520
There's no one else in the world

523
00:26:53,570 --> 00:26:55,790
I would ask to marry me three times.

524
00:26:58,140 --> 00:27:00,030
But I want to take care of you...

525
00:27:00,830 --> 00:27:02,190
...have babies with you...

526
00:27:03,590 --> 00:27:04,950
...and grow old with you.

527
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:10,950
Phoebe Buffay, will you marry me?

528
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:12,920
Yes.

529
00:27:20,020 --> 00:27:22,680
- I love you. - I love you more.

530
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:23,990
Not possible.

531
00:27:33,370 --> 00:27:35,380
She's gonna be Mrs. No Balls!

532
00:27:42,110 --> 00:27:45,460
So how's the baby-styling business going?

533
00:27:45,610 --> 00:27:47,100
Not that great.

534
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:48,990
It's almost as if people don't want

535
00:27:48,990 --> 00:27:51,290
to hear that their babies are ugly.

536
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:54,200
That's shocking.

537
00:27:55,570 --> 00:27:58,670
There's Ross. Hey, Ross.

538
00:28:00,820 --> 00:28:02,800
Hello, Ross?

539
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:06,650
He's rude.

